-- pg_turbovec 1.29.0 -- Partitioned-scale support + 1-bit foundation.
--
-- This file is a *reference mirror*. The authoritative install script
-- (including the new turbovec.partition_summary table and the two
-- partition functions) is generated by `cargo pgrx schema`.
--
-- MINOR bump: purely ADDITIVE SQL surface, no wire-format change
-- (MetaPageData::version stays 7), NO REINDEX. Existing indexes and
-- queries are unaffected; `ALTER EXTENSION pg_turbovec UPDATE TO
-- '1.29.0';` is sufficient and cannot fail on existing indexes.
--
-- Changes:
--
--   Phase S-0/S-1 (partitioned scale toward 1T+ vectors) -----------
--   pg_turbovec scales past PostgreSQL's ~11B-row single-table
--   ceiling via declarative hash-partitioning + per-partition
--   turbovec indexes; PG's native Merge Append already does correct,
--   LAZY global top-k across the partitions (proved: 10/10 overlap
--   vs a single-table exact scan). See docs/PARTITIONED_SCALE.md for
--   the cookbook (partition sizing, embarrassingly-parallel
--   per-partition build orchestration, insert routing, per-partition
--   VACUUM/REINDEX). Unlocks 1-10B vectors TODAY with no AM changes.
--
--   New SQL surface (Phase S-1 partition pruning, so a query fans out
--   to only the Kp nearest partitions instead of all N):
--     * turbovec.partition_summary               -- catalog table
--         (parent regclass, partition regclass, summary turbovec.vector, ...)
--     * turbovec.refresh_partition_summary(parent regclass, vec_col text)
--         RETURNS bigint  -- computes each partition's MEAN vector in
--         ORIGINAL (un-rotated) space (partitions train independent
--         rotations, so persisted per-partition centroids are NOT
--         cross-comparable; the mean is) and upserts summary rows.
--     * turbovec.nearest_partitions(parent regclass, query turbovec.vector,
--                                    k_partitions int, metric text)
--         RETURNS SETOF regclass  -- the Kp partitions whose summary is
--         closest to the query; the client fans out only to those.
--   Pruning turns O(N)-partition fan-out into O(Kp). Near-lossless for
--   content-clustered partitions; hash-partitioned means ~= the global
--   mean, so hash needs a larger Kp to hold recall (documented).
--
--   1-bit (sign binary quantization) FOUNDATION ---------------------
--   `WITH (bit_width = 1)` is now ACCEPTED by the reloption (range
--   1..=4; 1 = sign-BQ, 2/3/4 = TurboQuant), and the exact-heap-rerank
--   floor auto-widens for a 1-bit index (reusing the existing
--   hi_dim_rerank/search_k/oversample machinery). The sign-BQ core
--   (mean-centering -- the mandatory footgun fix for non-zero-centered
--   data -- + degenerate-all-same-sign detection + half-of-2-bit
--   storage) is implemented and unit-tested.
--   NOTE: the 1-bit BUILD path is NOT yet implemented -- a
--   `CREATE INDEX ... WITH (bit_width = 1)` ERRORs clearly
--   ("not yet implemented; use bit_width = 2, 3, or 4"), never
--   half-builds or ships a silent all-ones landmine. The end-to-end
--   1-bit encode/scan path (which requires a wire bump to v8) lands
--   in a later release after full validation. The reloption is
--   accepted now for forward compatibility only.
